{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a6ee5badc37477fc2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are an independent, BLIND critic in an adversarial review (\"gauntlet\") of a skill framework for autonomous AI agents that will build a brand-new game engine from scratch — from small 2D indie games to future AAA open-world online games. The framework is NOT the engine design: it is (1) a capability map of everything needed to build and ship the engine, (2) a hierarchy of skills owning those capabilities, (3) contracts between skills, (4) configurations proving scale-down, (5) a critic framework, radar, anti-legacy catalogue and milestone ladder. Each skill later becomes a SKILL.md for a specialized agent. You judge whether the framework is COMPLETE and CORRECTLY BOUNDED.\n\nARTIFACT — read ONLY inside this directory: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad/r2/engine-skill-framework/\n- data/*.json is the source of truth: capabilities.json ([id, name, owner, maturity E/M/X/S, contributors, capability-level profiles]), skills.json (kinds, targets, platforms, profiles, configurations, consumes / tool_consumes / implements, workstreams, untrusted_inputs, fuzz_targets), contracts.json, critics.json, crosscutting.json, seed-map.json, radar.json, legacy-patterns.json, milestones.json.\n- docs/00-design-principles.md (hand-written rationale — attack it), docs/01..05 and 09 (generated views), docs/06 gap analysis, 07 research plan, 08 phase-2 plan, gauntlet/PROTOCOL.md.\n- You may run `python3 scripts/check.py` there. It machine-proves: single existing owner per capability; every skill owns territory; acyclic, non-upward contract layering; no upward module links; tool contracts only consumed tool-side; acyclic bootstrap tier; closure of all 22 configurations (profiles × target × platform) and required implementers; milestone closure; leads own a contract; every skill has a domain critic; tool-logic and ML owners reach the editor / inference runtime through contracts; every non-established capability on the radar; brief terms map to real capabilities. It CANNOT tell whether an owner is the right one, whether something is missing, whether a boundary or label is wrong, or whether a stance is legacy — that is your job.\nBLIND RULE: do not read or search anything outside that directory (not the /home/user/skills repository, not other files in the scratchpad).\n\nTHE BAR (mission brief, condensed): support indie, 2D, 2.5D, modern 3D, open-world, multiplayer, large-scale simulation, high-end PC, console-class, current and future AAA; scale down as well as up. Best practice = strongest demonstrated approach today; techniques separated into established/emerging/experimental/speculative. Done means (among others): complete domain map; every domain owned; no unexplained overlap; explicit dependencies; cross-cutting (incl. security) represented; realistic coordination of many autonomous agents. The engine is built by autonomous AI agents.\n\nYOUR ROLE: Security Critic. Mandate: threat model and trust boundaries across every untrusted input (network packets, saves/cloud saves, mods/UGC and UGC graphs, scripts, assets and decompressors, fonts/text, media decoders, replays, remote config, invites/deep links, generated/LLM content, editor plugins and imported DCC files) — does each have a validating owner and a fuzz target (untrusted_inputs vs fuzz_targets)? Memory-safety posture and hardening; sandboxing (scripts, mods, plugins, UGC shaders/GPU DoS); supply chain and build integrity; secrets and signing-key custody; development-agent boundaries (least privilege, prompt injection, provenance); anti-cheat and server authority; network DoS; privacy and data rights (telemetry, crash dumps, player data, children's data); commerce/receipt security; vulnerability response and incident handling for the engine and shipped games; design-time security review coverage by critics.\n\nOUTPUT: write findings to /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad/r2/engine-skill-framework/gauntlet/round-2/K-SEC.md, one block per finding:\n### K-SEC-<n> · <blocker|major|minor> · <omission|overlap|wrong-boundary|wrong-owner|obsolete-assumption|missing-contract|dependency-error|maturity-error|scale-down|other>\n- Target: <ids>\n- Finding: <concrete deficiency>\n- Evidence: <technical reasoning; precedent (incidents, CVEs, standards) where possible>\n- Proposed change: <concrete data change>\nSeverity: blocker = framework cannot coordinate agents correctly; major = material omission/wrong boundary causing rework or real exposure; minor = small placement/naming issue. Only concrete, material findings within your mandate; no style, no praise, no padding; at most ~20, most severe first. If nothing material, say so explicitly. Final message: one line with counts by severity and the output path."},"uuid":"9dc3dd36-e642-479e-b5b9-c433dc619d2e","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:21:42.911Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
