{"parentUuid":"980bfed2-72af-4eeb-b253-55f2410c8302","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a6ee5badc37477fc2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EtHXJtYF9buQazy4y8ZfGn","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"id\": \"K-SEC\", \"name\": \"Security Critic\", \"mandate\": \"Threat model, trust boundaries, memory safety, supply chain, privacy, incident response \\u2014 reviewed at design time as well as in code.\", \"checks\": [\"every untrusted input has a validating owner and a fuzz target\", \"trust boundaries explicit\", \"hardening & key custody\", \"privacy of telemetry, crash and player data\"], \"scope\": [\"all\", \"subtree:security-engineering\", \"network-transport\", \"scripting-runtime\", \"modding-ugc\", \"plugin-system\", \"serialization-schema\", \"package-formats-vfs\", \"persistence-save\", \"platform-services\", \"online-services-liveops\", \"packaging-release-patching\", \"ci-cd-automation\", \"build-system-toolchains\", \"observability-telemetry\", \"crash-diagnostics\", \"editor-architect\", \"ai-assisted-authoring\", \"ai-behavior-perception\", \"dedicated-server\", \"asset-import-interchange\"], \"stages\": [\"G1\", \"G2\", \"S1\", \"S2\", \"S3\", \"S4\"]}\n{\"_doc\": \"Critic framework. scope selectors: 'all', 'tier:<tier>', 'subtree:<skill-id>' (the skill and all descendants), or a bare skill id. Stages: G1 = framework gauntlet (this phase; every critic reviews the whole framework), G2 = SKILL.md gauntlet (per-skill, scoped), S1 = ADR review, S2 = design/contract review, S3 = implementation review, S4 = validation & release review.\", \"stages\": {\"G1\": \"Framework gauntlet: capability map, skill graph, contracts, hierarchy (whole framework)\", \"G2\": \"SKILL.md gauntlet: per-skill description quality, technique currency, validation criteria\", \"S1\": \"ADR review: evidence, alternatives, revisit conditions\", \"S2\": \"Design & contract review: API/contract drafts, data layouts, threading model\", \"S3\": \"Implementation review: code, tests, instrumentation\", \"S4\": \"Validation & release review: benchmarks, scalability runs, certification readiness\"}}\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:23:| Cross-cutting | 11 | Disciplines that impose an obligation on every skill and review against it: research evidence, performance, testing, security, observability, crash diagnostics, determinism, hot reload, accessibility, API lifecycle, developer experience. |\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:68:- **Scale/feature profiles.** A base profile (`minimal`, `min2d`, `lite3d`, `std3d`) plus add-ons (`openworld`, `online`, `aaa`, `xr`, `ugc`, `massim`, `sandbox`, `vehicles`, `team-large`).\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:26:| A11 | Memory-safety posture for a C++ engine | Guidance exists (hardening modes, safe subsets, Rust interop), but there is little production evidence for engines specifically. | security-engineering, core-runtime-architect | ADR: which layers must accept untrusted input, and therefore get hardened containers, bounds checking in shipping builds and fuzzing. Evaluate Rust/Swift interop only for parsers of untrusted data. |\ndocs/06-gap-analysis.md:45:| B8 | Scripting | Luau/Lua vs .NET (C#) vs Wasm vs visual-only vs none | scripting-runtime | Console AOT constraints, sandboxing (mods), iteration speed, GC pauses, team skills. |\ndocs/07-research-plan.md:39:| **Testing & validation** | test-architect and quality experts | \"Automated Testing at Scale in Sea of Thieves\" (GDC 2019); FLIP image metric (Andersson et al., HPG 2020); libFuzzer/AFL++ docs; sanitizer docs (Clang); mutation-testing literature; platform certification checklists (licensed); Harding flash test / ITU-R BT.1702 (photosensitivity). |\ndocs/07-research-plan.md:41:| **Security** | security-engineering, anti-cheat-integrity | OWASP game-security material; CISA/NSA memory-safety guidance; SLSA; anti-cheat vendor integration docs (EAC, BattlEye) as boundary documents; GDPR, COPPA and regional privacy regulation texts. |\ndocs/08-phase-2-plan.md:34:| Constraints | performance, latency, determinism, memory, threading, platform, security, compatibility, scalability |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c54e94d0-46ef-4cf5-8710-e58e9ef520a8","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:22:52.091Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"980bfed2-72af-4eeb-b253-55f2410c8302","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
